  "description": "Read horizontal intersection coordinates and compare function heights on actual framed graphs.",
  "source": {
    "authoredBasis": "New written-source graph, not an original. Plot y=x^2 and y=x+2 on the same frame. Exact crossings (-1,1),(2,4); y=x^2 is below the line for -1<x<2 and above outside. Crossings and solution intervals are not labelled. No deliberate false geometry.",
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s3-n42",
        "exercise": "852",
        "text": "852. 用图解法解方程 $x^2=x+2$ 和不等式 $x^2<x+2$，$x^2>x+2$。"
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "panel-1",
        "description": "Authored panel P and L: both functions share the same x/y frame. No source image exists. Half-unit x grid and unit y grid, unlabelled crossings, and a dashed line versus solid exact parabola are new display aids. The line is clipped only at the plot boundary; no mathematical domain restriction is intended.",
